# Always use Python Virtual Environment

- Always use the project virtualenv interpreter. Never use system `python`, pyenv shims, or other global interpreters unless the user explicitly asks.
- Resolve: `<workspace-root>/.venv/bin/python` (then `<current-project-dir>/.venv/bin/python` if different). Use absolute paths.
- If no `.venv` exists, read and follow the **python-venv-bootstrap** skill before creating one.
